# Earflow Backend (Node.js)

Node 22+. Express services in `backend/*-service/`, workers in `backend/*-worker/`.

## Patterns

- CommonJS (`module.exports`) in existing services — follow local style
- DB: parameterized queries via pg pool; schemas in `backend/*.sql`
- Service auth: validate `X-Service-Token` / service JWT per `reports/SECURITY.md`
- Errors: structured JSON responses; log without leaking secrets or PII
- Health: expose `/health` or `/healthz` if service already has one

## Service boundaries

- `database-service` — catalog CRUD (not direct DB from other services in new code)
- `auth-service` / `security-service` — identity, MFA, sessions (Redis auth)
- `upload-service` — file intake → MinIO → processing pipeline

## Avoid

- Raw SQL string concatenation with user input
- Trusting client-sent `X-User-Id` (gateway sets this after session validation)
- New env vars without documenting in `.env.example`
